      ],
      "year": 2026,
      "abstract": "This third volume of the Handbook of Dynamic Data Driven Applications Systems (DDDAS) highlights DDDAS research spanning over two decades, with an emphasis on the key areas of theory, modeling, instrumentation, and applications examples, expanding the scope of work covered in the prior two volumes (Volume 1/2nd Edition and Volume 2) in this series. Research efforts under the rubric of DDDAS have demonstrated the successful use of the DDDAS paradigm for contemporary science and engineering systems as well as complex natural and societal systems. DDDAS-based methods foster advances through approaches where system-cognizant models, at execution time, “learn” from instrumentation and other data, and in return can leverage high-dimensional or abstract system-cognizant models to provide knowledge that augments real-time estimation, analysis, and control. Many examples are presented in this and the preceding two volumes that highlight recent approaches, designs, and uses of the DDDAS concept toward advancing science through data understanding, analysis, and discovery. Future efforts would further develop these DDDAS concepts toward a better understanding of scientific principles, engineering system design, and multi-domain applications. DDDAS advances leverage and influence areas such as: dynamic digital twins, machine learning analytics, multi-domain autonomy, and contextual awareness.",
      "abstract_not_available": false,
      "snippet": "This third volume of the Handbook of Dynamic Data Driven Applications Systems (DDDAS) highlights DDDAS research spanning over two decades, with an...",
