      "paperId": "/chapter/10.1007/978-3-032-19042-0_2",
      "doi": "10.1007/978-3-032-19042-0_2",
      "title": "Millimeter Wave and Terahertz Communication: An Overview",
      "authors": [
        {
          "name": "Poonam Maurya, Megha Sahu, ... M. K. Askar"
        }
      ],
      "year": 2026,
      "abstract": "This chapter serves to examine the demand for millimeter-wave (mmWave) and terahertz (THz) communication, while also delving into the obstacles, potential solutions, and practical applications associated with it. It offers a comprehensive understanding of the fundamentals of mmWave and THz communication, with a focus on promising applications and use cases across various industries. Despite the significant challenges, such as the limited range of propagation and the demanding efficient design requirements for antennas, this chapter discusses potential solutions to overcome these issues. Additionally, it delves into the growing security and privacy needs associated with mmWave and THz communication. Furthermore, it discusses the role of artificial intelligence (AI) and cloud computing in enhancing the efficiency of mmWave and THz communication systems. Lastly, it provides a forward-thinking outlook on the future of mmWave and THz communication, predicting ongoing innovation and implementation of these advanced technologies.",
